**glyph.hpp maps controller devices and keys to presentation glyph families and stable text labels.**

## Interface

`glyph_family : uint8_t` exports `xbox` and `playstation`.

`glyph_family_for(controller::family, optional<glyph_family>) noexcept` returns the override, otherwise `playstation` for PlayStation devices and `xbox` for all others.

`glyph_for(engine_key, glyph_family) noexcept` returns `const char*` labels such as `"BUTTON_A"` and `"DPAD_UP"`; `glyph_family` is API-compatible but ignored.

## Coupling

`types.hpp` supplies `optional`; `utility.hpp`, `key.hpp`, and `identity.hpp` supply shared mapping, key, and device-family types.